KG42.register("clusters-dc0a27fd6d562e8fd24cada6",{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v142-d-CL003","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","label":"Energy storage allocation and over-supply burden within the participating group","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"Energy storage allocation and over-supply burden within the participating group","market_meaning":"Given the participating group, the RU equilibrium supply, and the SFC demand, the auctioneer determines each RU's actual shared contribution; when supply is insufficient, its entire equilibrium supply is used, and when there is over-supply, the shared quantity is reduced according to the selected burden rule. The paper subsequently adopts equal burden, while price-proportional and quantity-proportional allocation are retained as different conditional configurations.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","matching","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The main assembly uses the group after excluding marginal participants and the equilibrium supply of the same auction. Equal, reserve-price-proportional, and shared-quantity-proportional allocations are different configurations, are not applied simultaneously, and are not mutually deleted as duplicate constraints. The branch allowing marginal participation and cross-time-slot updates cannot be directly applied to the current allocation expression.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"This cluster treats shared-quantity allocation and the over-supply burden as independent outcomes and references the screening output and price-response output as interfaces. The supply response is an allocation input, and the final allocation is not a synonymous object of the original response; the total-quantity closure after truncation and the SFC-side allocation are still missing, so it is retained as partial.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carry the auctioneer's allocation responsibility, the supply-demand branches, and the three burden configurations; this is the main attribution of the quantity allocation rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provide the participation cutoff and the group condition after excluding marginal parties; do not re-own or re-execute the participant screening rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provide the pricing and response source of the equilibrium supply; connect to allocation only at the level of the equilibrium realization value of the same participating group and the same auction."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-J","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-K"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-J","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-K"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E22"],"rationale":"The participation cutoff becomes a fixed input in the allocation stage and defines the participation scope for the allocation summation and equal burden; the variable and parameter roles in different stages remain separate."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"Marginal exclusion determines the participation scope of the truthful-auction branch, and equal burden is the allocation configuration subsequently adopted by the paper; the two are complementary, but this does not declare that truthfulness has been proven, nor does it treat the group-set expression and the necessary-condition statement as duplicate constraints."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-xi","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C007","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C008"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-xi-star","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E20"],"rationale":"In the source text, supply is first determined by price and RU response, and then allocation is performed using the equilibrium supply. The interface only takes up the equilibrium realization value under the selected price and does not regard the general quantity strategy, the equilibrium input, and the actual allocated quantity as the same object; the mathematical gap in pricing remains."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g01-E36"],"rationale":"Screening, pricing, and allocation are all undertaken by the auctioneer in the same mechanism; unified display does not merge different activities into a single scientific edge."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R005::V::matching.counterparties"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E07"],"rationale":"Both pricing and allocation reference the previously determined participating group; the shared node does not prove that re-matching will occur automatically after the equilibrium quantity changes."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-J","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-J","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-J"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E20"],"rationale":"The RU cutoff of the same auction runs through screening, pricing, and allocation; the distinction between decision output and stage input is retained, and it is not rewritten as the actual number of transacting participants."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-K","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-K","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-K"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E20"],"rationale":"The SFC cutoff of the same auction is used by pricing and allocation; local variables and parameters continue to be stored independently, and the marginal participation branch is not mixed in."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-r-i","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-r","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-ri"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E21"],"rationale":"The RU reserve price of the same auction is used in screening, utility, and the reserve-price-proportional burden configuration; this mapping does not make proportional burden an additional condition of the equal configuration."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Equal burden or reserve-price-proportional burden may exceed the equilibrium supply of an individual RU. After R001-C005 is truncated to zero, the total allocated quantity is not necessarily equal to total demand, and the original chain has no rule for reallocating the remaining over-supply; the sum of burdens being equal to the over-supply itself cannot guarantee quantity closure after truncation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-Qi","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-etai"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream shall check whether the burden is limited by each RU's supply and the total-quantity conservation conditions after truncation; determine whether the source specifies reallocation or restricts applicable conditions; this time no algorithm is fabricated."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R001-C001 describes allocating energy storage to each SFC, but the existing mathematics only gives each RU's shared contribution and provides neither per-SFC allocation nor an RU-to-SFC correspondence. The insufficient-supply branch also cannot be interpreted as meaning that all demand has been satisfied.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-qm"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E20"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream shall confirm the buyer-side allocation, the handling when demand is insufficient, and the quantity correspondence between the two sides; if the source does not specify these, the result should continue to be limited to an RU-side contribution candidate."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G03","category":"scope_conflict","description":"R004 allows marginal participants to be included when truthfulness is not required, but the existing expressions of R001 and R005 use the scope after excluding marginal parties. Equal burden is the configuration subsequently adopted by the paper; the other two proportional configurations cannot be applied simultaneously, nor can they inherit a truthfulness conclusion that has not been independently verified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C008","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E08","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Keep the main configuration separate from the conditional alternative configurations; if extending to the case where marginal participants are included, upstream shall provide the corresponding pricing, allocation scope, and basis for the properties."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G04","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The initial declared quantity when constructing the matching curve, the price-response strategy, the equilibrium supply, and the final shared contribution are at different stages. The source text supports entering allocation from the equilibrium supply, but the existing chains do not prove that these quantities are generally the same, nor do they specify re-determining the participating group after the response changes.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-xi","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-xi-star","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-Qi"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E20"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream shall specify the quantities at each stage and their transfer conditions; continue to retain only the equilibrium realization value interface, and do not establish unconditional same-quantity mappings among these quantities or automatic re-matching dependencies."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G05","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R001 and R005 mention per-time-slot application, but the current chains do not incorporate the cross-time-slot supply and demand updates from the source text; the quantity roles and participant indices in the time-varying citations also cannot be directly equated with static objects. Therefore this assembly does not cover a complete time-varying auction.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-xi-star","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-qm","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E26","v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33","v141-b-g02-E34"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If time-varying rules are to be assembled, upstream shall separately extract the state updates, initial conditions, and time-slot indices, verify the participant set and quantity roles, and then connect them; a dynamic closed loop must not be supplied merely on the basis of a statement about per-time-slot reuse."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G06","category":"ontology_extension","description":"What this cluster allocates is a share of energy storage space or capacity use; the mere mixed use of the word energy in the source text cannot lead to identifying it as actually delivered electrical energy. The related capacity product proposal has still not been approved, and the interpretation of units and shares cannot be uniformly rewritten during assembly.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-Qi","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-xi-star","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-qm","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-xi"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g03-e07"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-P01","v141-b-g02-P01","v141-b-g03-p01"],"required_work":"Manual review shall check the capacity product proposal, quantity units, and share basis; before approval, retain the original parameter meanings and units, and do not insert capacity nodes or change mappings into electrical energy trading."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G07","category":"unverified_source","description":"The allocation formula, burden configurations, and basis for per-time-slot reuse all come from the currently unverified B evidence. Their candidate availability does not constitute independent confirmation of quantity conservation, strategy truthfulness, or temporal relations.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E26"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequent manual review shall check the original formulas, conditions, and candidate interfaces; continue to retain all frozen objects and the existing source_status."}]},"rule_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R004","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-72f84a438787fbd5","COMP-bebd346528bbcf18","COMP-c98744ae891e04fd","KG31-e2bea6d6e2936fab","KG40-404d7eddbf0fc37c"]});
